From the section connecting the annotations drawn from other textual examples of the Four Tantras, the following becomes clear. Likewise, in the explanation contained within the Four Tantras: from the treatise entitled "The Oral Instruction Tantra that Prophesies Proficiency in the Four Tantras," page 532:

Regarding the experiential oral instructions: the terminology concerning what is and is not found in the textual sources of the Four Tantras on medical and astrological examples; the defining characteristics of a teacher who should be relied upon by one who wishes to become learned in medicine and astrology;

The logical proofs establishing where something is grounded or not grounded; the rituals of cultivating medicinal and astrological fields; and the relevant knowledge pertaining to the appropriate time for cultivation;

Regarding the oral instructions on the synthesis of truth: the methods of treatment employed by the physician; the oral instructions on the taste and essence of the three qualities of warmth, heat, and cold; and the practical application of substances such as elm, oak, and butter, and so forth;

Regarding the oral instructions on the two of comfort and suffering: the methods for purifying bodily impurities; the methods for properly maintaining one's dwelling and bedding; and the transmission of scriptural authority for the purposes of practice;

Regarding the oral instructions of the Comfort Tantra: kashi, kure, shudak, the work of sha, gyub, drag-tha, gyub-kyi, shu-zhi, shamyar, chungyar, kabyar, kuryar, shamyar, druyar, kabyar, triyar, mi.
